Robotic Cryobiopsy 2022
Chapter heading placeholder
Abstract
Robotic cryobiopsy expands access to peripheral lung lesions.
Methods
A retrospective cohort of 112 patients with 120 lesions was analysed.
Results
The diagnostic yield was 90% with 101/112 diagnostic specimens.
Pneumothorax occurred in 5% of cases and bleeding in 2%.
Table 1 Diagnostic Yield
Category | Cases | Percent
Malignant | 90 | 85
Benign | 11 | 10
Non-diagnostic | 11 | 5
Conclusions
Robotic cryobiopsy is feasible.
References
1. Smith J. Robotic cryobiopsy outcomes. Journal of Lung 2022;10(2):100-110. doi:10.1234/abcd.2022.10
2. Doe A. Complications of cryobiopsy. Chest Medicine 2021;9(1):90-95. PMID 123456
